  "verdict": "YES: the propagated 1-sigma timing uncertainty (24.8 h in S6, 17.9 h in S32 with the adopted bootstrap sigma; 10.9 h and 7.8 h with the likelihood-only sigma) is 4-13 times the 1.87 h transit duration. The +-3 sigma window covers the whole 76 h orbit (adopted) or 62-86 % of it (likelihood). The prediction centre misses the archival transits by 12.9 h (S6) and 9.3 h (S32) = 0.5 sigma; the discovery-record centre misses by 3.1 h and 2.2 h (0.1 sigma); both misses exceed T14/2."
