 "caveats": [
  "The prediction is weak: S98-only P estimates range 3.18164-3.18276 d across methods (this fit 3.18211); propagated over ~800 cycles the uncertainty is 4-13 x T14, so \"at the predicted time\" really means \"at the predicted period, anywhere in most of the phase\".",
  "All S98-only fits except the discovery record were made after the first archival look (04:45 CEST); this one too (rule fixed in the script before running, S98 data only).",
  "Per-sector FAPs are upper bounds set by the ~160-195 independent null periods available in one sector; counting 0/20 000 as independent (5e-5, 3.9 sigma) would overstate the evidence.",
  "S/N is in white-noise units; red noise is handled only through the empirical nulls (N1 null SD 1.06 in S6, 1.41 in S32).",
  "S32 null tail is set by segment-edge detrending artefacts (single box S/N up to 11 at the sector end); the observed S32 value barely exceeds the null maximum without an edge cut.",
  "S6 momentum dumps (every 3.125 d) lie 0.4-3.5 h from every S6 A transit. Boxes 0.4-3.6 h from dumps (true transits removed) show mean S/N -0.71 (brightening side), SD 0.93, vs -0.05 / 1.06 far from dumps, so dumps do not manufacture dips; only ~8 independent dump-adjacent boxes, so this check is weak. The N2r null (P' 3.10-3.26 d, including dump-aligned trains) has lower maxima than N2.",
  "Detrending: biweight 0.5/0.75/1.0 d and a 0.375 d edge cut change the optimised S/N by -1.1/+0.7 (joint 12.1-13.9) and never produce a null exceedance.",
  "A is never masked in the archival detrending (same for all trials); this shrinks box depths by ~7-9 % (S6 422 vs 454 ppm masked).",
  "Depth ratio uses box depths; the S98 epoch -1 event (data-gap edge) drags the S98 box depth from 389 to 299 ppm; ratios quoted without it."
 ],
